{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"primary decomposition of ideals primary decomposition of ideals","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md","fileName":"Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Primary Decomposition of Ideals","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-13 19:40\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra","Ideal","Primary Ideal","Noetherian Ring","Prime Ideal","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"primary decomposition of ideals primary decomposition of ideals","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md","fileName":"Primary Decomposition of Ideals.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Primary Decomposition of Ideals","heading":"Primary Decomposition of Ideals","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A primary decomposition writes an [[Ideal]] as a finite intersection of [[Primary Ideal]]s. In a [[Noetherian Ring]], every ideal has such a decomposition.\n\nTaking radicals of the primary components reveals the associated [[Prime Ideal]]s, while the primary components retain information analogous to prime powers. The construction generalizes unique prime-power decomposition from integers to broader commutative rings.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Prime Ideals and Noetherian Algebra","Ideal","Primary Ideal","Noetherian Ring","Prime Ideal","commutativealgebra.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd